    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maintenance cost per volume of water delivered to users in project area</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2002-12-31" value="Actual expenditure of 153 US$ per 1000 cum deliver" year="2002">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2002-12-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2012-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="45 US$ per 1000 cum delivered to users">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target not met because the expenditure is not likely to secure long-term functionality of the infrastructure.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="The expenditure for maintenance of the public irri">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The expenditure for maintenance is still much below the estimated cost of associated with regular maintenance activities to securelong-term functionality of the irrigation infrastructure (canals and pump stations). However, it is likely that expenditure formaintenance to gradually increase towards meeting the reasonable costs, once the farmers started understanding the risks of newdepreciation of the rehabilitated infrastructure. The maintenance tariffs for 2012 increased. Meeting the target would take moretime than the remaining project life.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
